## 19. MoLingo Diagnostic Benchmark Evaluation

Automatic Pass / Fail / Unclear labels.
Reads molingo_sample1_repeat0.npy … sample13 (T2M joints, not mp4/gif), writes one row per atomic requirement, and reports ARA. Human gold is filled after the GRID GIFs.
` Trajectory Tracking (extract_signals / judge_direction)`

Calculates the horizontal and depth displacement of the pelvis between the first frame and the last frame (ΔX, ΔZ). Turn clips use an early window so a later right turn does not overwrite “walks forward”. This detects whether the locomotion path went forward, backward, left, or right.

` Torso Turn Control (judge_turn)`

Measures the unwrapped yaw of the hips and shoulders from the start of the clip to the end (Δθ). After the Week 9 X-mirror, a right turn faces +X and Δθ is positive. This identifies a sharp left turn, a right turn, or no turn.

` Action Counting (find_peaks on root Y)`

Tracks the vertical displacement of the pelvis relative to the first frame. Upward peaks count jumps. The same height signal is reused for Count (jump once / jump twice) on prompts 2, 8, 9, and 12.

` Arm Height and Body Side (judge_action / Body Side / Arm Direction)`

Compares left wrist (joint 20) and right wrist (joint 21) against the head (joint 15). Wrist ΔY decides left vs right. Wrist−head clearance and frames-above-head decide Arm Direction = up.

` Attribute Control (mean_speed)`

Mean horizontal pelvis speed from root XZ and frame rate. Slow vs fast on prompts 6 and 7.

` Temporal Structure (judge_order / Simultaneous / Paraphrase)`

Order timestamps walk / jump / turn. Simultaneous measures overlap between walking frames and a raised right hand. Paraphrase Pair checks that prompt 13 agrees with prompt 11.

` The Table Loop (evaluate)`

Maps each JSON-style atomic requirement onto the observed signals, writes Pass / Fail / Unclear per row and prints suite ARA (Unclear excluded). This run: 37/46 = 80.4%.
"""

